{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-2794","published":"2026-06-24T11:11:43Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:12.568154526Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-55203","CVE-2026-55204"],"summary":"haproxy security update","details":"HAProxy is a free, very fast and reliable solution offering high availability, load balancing, and proxying for TCP and HTTP-based applications. It is particularly suited for very high traffic web sites and powers quite a number of the world&amp;apos;s most visited ones.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nHAProxy through 3.4.0, fixed in commit 5985276, contains an integer overflow vulnerability in the fcgi_conn structure&apos;s drl field that allows buffer misparse as new FCGI record headers. When contentLength is 65535 and paddingLength is 1 or more, the drl field wraps to 0, causing incorrect record consumption and allowing malicious FastCGI backends to desynchronize the FCGI framing parser, potentially causing request routing errors, response smuggling, or memory safety issues.(CVE-2026-55203)\n\nHAProxy through  3.4.0, fixed in commit 9a6d1fe, contains a null pointer dereference vulnerability in hpack_dht_insert() within src/hpack-tbl.c that fails to validate the return value of hpack_dht_defrag() when the memory pool is exhausted. An attacker can trigger HPACK dynamic table insertions under memory pressure to dereference a NULL pointer and crash HAProxy worker processes, causing denial of service.(CVE-2026-55204)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"haproxy","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/haproxy&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["haproxy-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","haproxy-debuginfo-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","haproxy-debugsource-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["haproxy-help-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["haproxy-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["haproxy-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","haproxy-debuginfo-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","haproxy-debugsource-2.2.16-10.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-2794.json"}},{"package":{"name":"haproxy","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/haproxy&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["haproxy-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","haproxy-debuginfo-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","haproxy-debugsource-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["haproxy-help-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["haproxy-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["haproxy-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","haproxy-debuginfo-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","haproxy-debugsource-2.6.6-20.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-2794.json"}},{"package":{"name":"haproxy","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/haproxy&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["haproxy-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","haproxy-debuginfo-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","haproxy-debugsource-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["haproxy-help-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["haproxy-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["haproxy-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","haproxy-debuginfo-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","haproxy-debugsource-2.9.5-14.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-2794.json"}},{"package":{"name":"haproxy","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/haproxy&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.0.11-3.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific